{
  "title": "Share extension can hang indefinitely on slow scrape",
  "description": "`RamekinShareExtension/ShareViewController.swift` fires \
`scrapeURL` with no timeout. The underlying `URLSession` default timeout is \
60s, but share extensions have a much tighter (~30s) memory/time budget before \
iOS terminates them. If the server is slow the user is stuck on the spinner \
until the OS kills the extension, with no error. Set \
`URLSessionConfiguration.default.timeoutIntervalForRequest = 15` on the share \
path (`scrape` only submits a job, so it should return fast), and surface a \
\"Still working, tap to close\" affordance after ~10s.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
    "share-extension",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-04-17T12:00:00-07:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-17T12:00:00-07:00",
}
